<title>MALAYSIA: Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur tin market is closed on Thursday for the Labour Day holiday.</p>
<p>The market reopens on May 2.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, Malaysia's tin price fell six cents to 14.05 ringgit ($5.60) a kg after players took their cue from an overnight fall on London Metal Exchange (LME), traders said.</p>
<p>Turnover rose to 110 tonnes from 88 tonnes on Tuesday. The premium over the LME widened widened to $100 from $70.</p>
</text>
